  "raw_text": "306\n\nKaia\n \n–\n \nPlural Person / Kaia\n \n–\n \nP\nersona\n \nP\nlural\n\nThe plural person of the verb\n \nKaia\n \n(\nto be\n) is formed by using\n \nBanhwi\n \nfollowed by the appropriately conjugated\n\nKaia\n \nverb. /\n\nLa persona plural del verbo\n \nKaia\n \n(ser/estar) se forma usando\n \nBanhwi\n \nseguido del verbo\n \nKaia\n \nadecuadamente\n\nconjugado.\n\nPresent /\nPresente\n\nPast I /\nPasado I\n\nPast II /\nPasado II\n\nFuture I /\nFuturo I\n\nFuture II /\nFuturo II\n\nYang (1\nst\n/1\ner\n)\n \nSna\n \nKatna\n \nKapri\n \nKaisna\n \nKamna\n\nMan (2\nnd\n/2\ndo\n)\n \nSma\n \nKatma\n \nKapram\n \nKaisma\n \nKama\n\nWitin(3\nrd\n/3\ner\n),Yawan\n \nSa\n \nKata\n \nKan\n \nKaisa\n \nKabia\n\nYang nani (1\nst\n/1\ner\n)\n \nBanhwi sna\n \nBanhwi katna\n \nBanhwi kapri\n \nBanhwi kaisna\n \nBanhwi kamna\n\nMan nani (2\nnd\n/2\ndo\n)\n \nBanhwi sma\n \nBanhwi katma\n \nBanhwi kapram\n \nBanhwi kaisma\n \nBanhwi kama\n\nWitin nani (3\nrd\n/3\ner\n)\n \nBanhwi sa\n \nBanhwi kata\n \nBanhwi kan\n \nBanhwi kaisa\n \nBanhwi kabia\n\nImperative/Imperativa:\n \nBas\n,\n \nBanhwi bas\n\nImperative including speaker/Imperativa incluido el hablante:\n \nKap\n,\n \nBanhwi kap\n\nProhibitive/Prohibitiva:\n \nKapara\n\nNegative/Negativa:\n \nKapras\n\nP\nresent participle/\n \nP\narticipio\n \npresente\n:\n \nSi\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\nYang nani banhwi sna\n \n–\n \nwe are\n \n/ nosotros somos\n\nMan nani banhwi sma\n \n–\n \nyou (plural) are\n \n/ ustedes son\n\nWitin nani banhwi sa\n \n–\n \nthey are\n \n/ ellos son\n\nYang nani banhwi kapri\n \n–\n \nwe were\n \n/ éramos\n\nMan nani banhwi kapram\n \n–\n \nyou (plural) were\n \n/ ustedes fueron\n\nWitin nani banhwi kan\n \n–\n \nthey were\n \n/ ellos eran\n\nYang nani banhwi kamna\n \n–\n \nwe will be\n \n/ nosotros seremos\n\nMan nani banhwi kama\n \n–\n \nyou (plural) will be\n \n/ ustedes serán\n\nWitin nani banhwi kabia\n \n–\n \nthey will be\n \n/ ellos serán",
